responding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}+4{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}+4{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3} & =4{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}} & =-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428955 #edb/ref 1030 0.3333333333333333 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428955 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [3]; waits [3]. Separate account estimates: differential=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/differential-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3198->6382. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428955 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186048443 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186432914 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "54b97394-ead1-526b-8c32-cf56b7a9ff77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432